[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The mswitch0↔router16 interconnect (r16_ms0 and r16_ms0_2) is healthy; there is no link failure to confirm. On mswitch0, both member interfaces toward router16 show physical carrier and are enslaved to the bond: ethtool reports “Link detected: yes” on eth0 and eth1, and ip addr shows eth0 and eth1 as SLAVE, UP, LOWER_UP under bond0, with bond0 itself UP/LOWER_UP. On router16, the corresponding interfaces eth0 and eth1 also report “Link detected: yes” via ethtool and appear as SLAVE, UP, LOWER_UP under bond0. Furthermore, layer-3 adjacency is functioning: router16 has 10.2.2.1/24 on bond0, and mswitch0 has 10.2.2.2/24 on br0 with multiple OSPF-learned routes installed via 10.2.2.1, indicating an active routing session across this link. If this bundle were down, we would see DOWN/NO-CARRIER on at least one side and loss of OSPF routes on mswitch0, which is not the case. Localization: mswitch0 eth0/eth1 to router16 eth0/eth1, aggregated as bond0 on both devices, are up. Root cause: not a physical/link issue between mswitch0 and router16. Corrective fix: none required on this link; investigate upstream of router16 (e.g., routing/OSPF toward router7/backbone or policy/filtering) for the loss of reachability beyond Campus 1. === END ===